%S A400854 24,120,168,240,264,840,0,480,504,1320,552,1680,0,696,1848,2040,0,
%T A400854 2520,0,2640,1176,2760,1128,3360,0,1272,3192,3480,1416,9240,0,4080,
%U A400854 3864,0,1704,10920,0,0,1896,5280,1992,5880,0,5520,5544,5640,0,14280
%N A400854 Largest k such that A046073(k) = n, or 0 if no such k exists.
%C A400854 If the multiplicative group of integers modulo k is of the form C_{2m_1} X ... X C_{2m_r}, with m_1 | m_2 | ... | m_r, then the number of squares modulo k is A046073(k) = m_1*...*m_r. In particular, any k with A046073(k) = n must divide A079612(2*n).
%C A400854 For squarefree n > 1, A046073(k) = n if and only if the multiplicative group of integers modulo k is of the form (C_2)^r X C_{2n} (cf. A400852).
%C A400854 Every term is divisible by 24, since k' = lcm(k,24) satisfies A046073(k') = A046073(k).
%H A400854 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400854/b400854.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1889</a>
%H A400854 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399566/a399566.txt">List of k such that A046073(k) = n <= 1889</a>.
%o A400854 (PARI) v(n) = select(x->A046073(x)==n, divisors(A079612(2*n))); \\ Gives the list of k such that A046073(k) = n; see A046073 and A079612 for their PARI programs. Warning: This is very inefficient since A079612(2*n) can easily have tens of millions of divisors. For squarefree n, it is much more advised to use multgp() given in the link of the PARI program for A400852.
%o A400854 A400854(n) = my(list=v(n)); return(if(list, vecmax(list), 0));
%Y A400854 Cf. A399566, A400862, A046073, A079612, A400852.
%K A400854 nonn,new
%O A400854 1,1
%A A400854 _Jianing Song_, Oct 07 2026
